attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a single spine column.** Column 0, `cspH`, is carried by 100% of chromosomes, persistent, in a region of plasticity in 77% of calls {S1}. The model names 99% of them, at 0.30 bits {S1, M}.

@variable **The rest of the window is fork and variable columns**, 1 to 79, carried by 58 to 90%, 65 persistent and 14 shell {S2}. A branch of 3 families runs through columns 2 to 4, `ymcF` to `gnsA`, in 10% {S2.b2}. The `hya` genes, columns 12 to 17, are [[hydrogenase formation]] {S2.c5-71, Q}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine column than on the fork and variable ones**, 99 against 94%, and hesitates more there, 0.30 against 0.26 bits {M}. Its most hesitant column, 48, `elfC`, is a variable column, at 0.71 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends on fork columns.** Columns 72 to 79, `ycaQ` to `ycaL`, are carried by 76 to 84%, all persistent {S2.c72-79}. The last column is `ycaL`, in 76% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 94% of genes**, 0.26 bits on average, perplexity 1.4 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 0.89 against 0.12 bits, and names fewer genes, 80% against 97% {C}.

